§C verdict
  ◐ ACCEPT_BOUNDED_LOCAL_CONCRETE_TYPECHECK_GATE.
  ✓ csslc.check+build now reject proven local concrete type errors before new artifact emission.
  ✓ valid bool `!` + legacy integer `!`|`~` + LanguageProfile remain accepted.
  N! global.type.soundness.claim.
  OPEN resolver.boundary := {
    imported bindings→Ty.Error opacity,
    qualified external paths→Ty.Error opacity,
    Option|Result|Ok|Err prelude surfaces→Ty.Error opacity,
    external signatures+cross-module unification=unresolved
  }.
  strongest.counterexample := `use external::opaque ; fn f() -> bool { opaque() }`
    may pass local gate because imported result domain is unknown/Ty.Error ; N! proven Bool.
  ✓ countercase.containment := unknown unqualified local name remains fatal ; any concrete
    local Bool violation remains fatal even when opaque imports+qualified paths coexist.
  OPEN artifact.identity := pre-existing output path remains untouched on refusal ; callers
    must N! treat stale artifact as current build output.
  excluded := {
    full imported|qualified|prelude resolution,
    full Bool-domain|foreign-ABI normalization,
    non-Cranelift Bool backend parity,
    vector runtime promotion,
    deployment|release|cutover
  }.
  falsifier := any concrete local negative above returns success|writes new object ; any
    accepted unary contract changes ; any main|aux bypasses check_module ; diagnostic lacks
    source coordinate ; LanguageProfile|native oracle|package regression fails.
